  10.7s | {"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cej4b7pdcAKUnekwHj2CH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Which cache backend do you want?\n\n**A. In-process memory** — a dict/LRU inside the app process. No new infra, fastest reads, but cache is per-instance and dies on restart.\n\n**B. Redis** — separate server, shared across instances, TTLs and eviction built in, plus pub/sub for invalidation. Needs hosting/ops.\n\n**C. Memcached** — separate server, shared, simpler and leaner than Redis for pure key/value blob caching, but no persistence or rich data types.\n\n**D. Database-backed table** — a cache table in your existing DB. Zero new infra and survives restarts, but it adds load to the thing you're probably trying to protect.\n\n**E. HTTP/CDN layer** — cache at the edge (Cloudflare/Varnish/`Cache-Control`) instead of in app code. Great for public GET responses, useless for per-user or internal computations.\n\nWaiting on your pick before I touch anything."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7924,"cache_read_input_tokens":9706,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7924},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"71ae13d2-f219-4059-8daf-60844ef82aed","uuid":"9aebb13d-61fa-4f2b-b33a-9d773da77dcc","timestamp":"2026-09-04T20:53:06.046Z","request_id":"req_011Cej4b721VPM4CYmyU2L8V"}
